---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Trace Commons and the Near.ai app collect, how it is used and shared, how long it is kept, and the choices you have."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <style is:inline>
      .page .toc {
        border: var(--hairline);
        padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
        max-width: 68ch;
      }
      .page .toc ol {
        columns: 2;
        column-gap: 2.5rem;
        margin: 0;
      }
      .page .toc li { break-inside: avoid; }
      .page h2, .page h3 { scroll-margin-top: var(--space-4); }
      @media (max-width: 560px) {
        .page .toc ol { columns: 1; }
      }
    </style>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information Iqlusion Inc. ("we",
    "us") collects when you use Trace Commons: the Near.ai desktop app
    (macOS, Windows and Linux), the contributor tools, the Trace Commons
    servers, and the tracecommons.ai websites (together, the "services").
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Effective [EFFECTIVE DATE]. By using the services you agree to this
    policy and to the <a href="/about/tnc">terms</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="banner">
    The short version: the app works on your computer first. Your code,
    prompts and coding sessions stay on your computer unless you choose to
    share a trace. Insights are computed on your computer. If you are in
    the United States, the app sends anonymous weekly counts of which
    screens you open, and you can turn that off in Settings. We do not sell
    your personal information.
  </div>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
    <p class="label">Contents</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#collect">Information we collect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#local">What stays on your computer</a></li>
      <li><a href="#use">How we use information</a></li>
      <li><a href="#share">How we share information</a></li>
      <li><a href="#retention">How long we keep it</a></li>
      <li><a href="#choices">Your choices and rights</a></li>
      <li><a href="#international">Where data is processed</a></li>
      <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
      <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="collect">Information we collect</h2>

  <h3>Account and sign-in</h3>
  <p>
    When you join, we create an account and record the sign-in you used: a
    NEAR AI login, a NEAR account, or an invite. We store identifiers for
    that sign-in in a form we can match on later (for example a hashed
    login identifier), the devices you enroll, and the dates they were
    added or removed. We do not receive your NEAR AI password.
  </p>

  <h3>Traces you choose to share</h3>
  <p>
    A trace is a record of a coding agent session. Traces are cleaned on
    your computer before they are sent: secrets and personal details the
    redaction finds are removed. A trace is sent only for projects you
    allow, either after you approve it or automatically for folders you
    set to Automatic. Each trace carries the consent options you chose,
    which limit how it may be used. What each option permits is set out in
    the <a href="/about/data-policy">data policy</a>. Redaction can miss
    things, so do not share sessions that contain information you would
    not want stored.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you turn on the optional extra privacy filter, already-cleaned
    message text is sent to a filter running in a protected enclave before
    upload. Structured tool data does not take that path.
  </p>

  <h3>Credits and payouts</h3>
  <p>
    For accepted traces we record credit, payout links you set up (for
    example the NEAR AI organization that receives credit), and the
    payouts made. Trace Credits are recorded on NEAR.
  </p>

  <h3>Private AI</h3>
  <p>
    If you use Private AI, the app sends your coding tools' AI requests
    through NEAR AI, which answers them. The app keeps a log of those
    requests on your computer. We receive which tools and models you
    connect and the credit used, not the content of your requests. NEAR
    AI's own privacy policy covers what it processes.
  </p>

  <h3>App usage data (United States only)</h3>
  <p>
    If our server places your connection in the United States, the app
    counts how many times a week you open each main tab and each Insights
    view, use Insights' Refresh and Analyze, and finish setup. It sends
    those weekly counts with a random identifier created for that install,
    which lets us tell how many installs come back. The identifier is not
    linked to your account, devices, email, name or files. No code, prompts,
    file names, folder names or trace content are ever part of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is on by default in the United States. Turn it off in Settings &gt;
    General &gt; Share anonymous usage data; that deletes the unsent counts
    and the identifier. Outside the United States, the app does not send
    usage data.
  </p>

  <h3>Technical information</h3>
  <p>
    Like most online services, our servers record the IP address, time and
    request path of connections, and the app version, to run the service,
    limit abuse and fix problems. We use the IP address to tell whether a
    connection is in the United States; we do not store the result with
    the address. The app keeps error logs on your computer and does not
    send them to us unless you choose to.
  </p>

  <h3>Website</h3>
  <p>
    The tracecommons.ai sites show public aggregates and the profiles of
    contributors who chose public attribution. They do not use advertising
    or cross-site tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <h3>When you contact us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we keep the message and your address to reply.
  </p>

  <h2 id="local">What stays on your computer</h2>
  <p>
    The app reads your coding tools' session files on your computer. Until
    you share a trace, that content stays there. Insights (your usage
    charts, breakdowns and analyses) are computed and stored on your
    computer and are not sent to us. Uninstalling the app does not remove
    traces you already shared; see <a href="#choices">your choices</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To run the services: accounts, uploads, checks on shared traces, credits and payouts.</li>
    <li>To use shared traces only as their consent options allow, as described in the <a href="/about/data-policy">data policy</a>.</li>
    <li>To understand how the app is used and improve it, from anonymous usage counts.</li>
    <li>To keep the services secure, prevent fraud and abuse, and enforce the <a href="/about/tnc">terms</a>.</li>
    <li>To reply to you, and to tell you about changes to the services or this policy.</li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="share">How we share information</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information or share it for advertising. We share it only:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>With service providers</strong> who run the services for us, such as cloud hosting, storage and key management, under contracts that limit their use to our instructions.</li>
    <li><strong>With NEAR AI</strong>, for sign-in, Private AI requests you send through it, and credit and payouts.</li>
    <li><strong>As your consent options allow</strong>, for shared traces, including use by others where an option you chose permits it.</li>
    <li><strong>Publicly</strong>, only your handle, bio and aggregate counts if you opt into public attribution.</li>
    <li><strong>For legal reasons</strong>, when the law requires it or to protect rights, safety and the services.</li>
    <li><strong>In a business transfer</strong>, such as a merger or acquisition, under this policy's protections.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account records: while your account is active, and for [RETENTION PERIOD] after it is closed.</li>
    <li>Shared traces: until you withdraw them. Withdrawing deletes our stored content and stops future use; copies already distributed under your consent options cannot be recalled.</li>
    <li>Credit, payout and audit records: as long as needed to keep the ledger correct and meet legal obligations.</li>
    <li>App usage counts: [RETENTION PERIOD].</li>
    <li>Server connection logs: [RETENTION PERIOD].</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="choices">Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose per project whether traces are shared, and which consent options apply.</li>
    <li>Withdraw shared traces from the app.</li>
    <li>Turn usage data off in Settings.</li>
    <li>Turn public attribution on or off on your <a href="/profile">profile</a>.</li>
    <li>Ask us to access, correct or delete your personal information, or to close your account, by emailing <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, including California, you may have rights
    to know what we collect, to delete or correct it, and to opt out of its
    sale or sharing. We do not sell or share personal information for
    advertising. We will not treat you differently for using these rights.
  </p>

  <h2 id="international">Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>
    We are based in the United States and process data there. If you use
    the services from elsewhere, your information is transferred to and
    processed in the United States.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    The services are not for anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly
    collect information from them. If you believe a child has given us
    information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    We encrypt stored traces and protect our systems with access controls
    and key management. No service is completely secure, and redaction on
    your computer can miss sensitive details.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The date at the top is when the published
    version took effect. If a change is significant, we will tell you in
    the app or by email before it applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions and requests:
    <a href="mailto:[PRIVACY EMAIL]">[PRIVACY EMAIL]</a>.<br />
    Iqlusion Inc., [POSTAL ADDRESS].
  </p>
  <p>
    See also the <a href="/about/privacy">privacy notes</a> for the public
    site, the <a href="/about/data-policy">data policy</a> and the
    <a href="/about/tnc">terms</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
